Z||000000||hugh||11-09-2000||07:33 AM||||I've been married to my best friend for 39 years today.She never complains when I work too many hours,even though I know she doesn't like it.If I want something for myself she never says we could use the money on something better.I can have anything I want with no questions asked. I have a lot of toys(dragster,show car,Grand National,88 Fiero GT).All she has is me,but she can have anything she wants.The only thing is,I am slow in delivering what she asks for.In 39 years we have never had an argument,we have been mad at each other but have never hollered at one another.I guess some people would consider this bragging,and I am,I guess.I feel so lucky to have found the one person in this world that could make me happy over such a long period of time and not want to change a single thing in my life.A side benefit is ,4 of my 5 children are happily married and the 5th is single but is seeing someone nice. I believe this is because of their relationship with their parents.I kiddingly said to my oldest daughter one day"You guys don't love me".Her reply"Sure we do dad,We just don't respect you" If this post got any longer Cliff might charge me.Thanks for listening. HUGH    ||||reg||1
